		<content type="html" xml:base="https://pybullet.org/Bullet/phpBB3/viewtopic.php?p=1547#p1547"><![CDATA[
There is definately room for improvements in Bullet, especially in performance optimizations. But 7 seconds startup for ~200 objects sounds like a bug.<br>The CcdPhysicsDemo has 120 objects, and starts without delay. Usually the broadphase cost is very minor compared to narrowphase.<br><br>Do you have a contribution, so we can compare timings? The <a href="http://www.continuousphysics.com/Bullet/phpBB2/viewtopic.php?t=469" class="postlink">previous posting</a> has details how to add timings.<br><br>Thanks a lot,<br>Erwin<p>Statistics: Posted by <a href="https://pybullet.org/Bullet/phpBB3/memberlist.php?mode=viewprofile&amp;u=2">Erwin Coumans</a> — Sat Aug 19, 2006 1:31 am</p><hr />
]]></content>
