		<link href="https://pybullet.org/Bullet/phpBB3/viewtopic.php?p=1545#p1545"/>
		<title type="html"><![CDATA[Slow AxisSweep3 startup]]></title>

		
		<content type="html" xml:base="https://pybullet.org/Bullet/phpBB3/viewtopic.php?p=1545#p1545"><![CDATA[
I found that the first and possibly second calls to PerformDiscreteCollisionDetection with AxisSweep3 are very slow if I have ca. &gt; 150-200 collision objects. The time for the first calls seems to explode with the number of objects. I get e.g. times of 7 seconds, while later calls need only 8 milliseconds. The time is apparently burned in the Sort... routines in AxisSweep3.<br><br>I built my own broadphase using Opcode, and this doesn't show such a behaviour. But Opcodes Sweep and Prune  is generally much faster, I am getting average times of 0.3 milliseconds vs. 8 milliseconds with AxisSweep3.<br>Perhaps there is some room for improvement.<p>Statistics: Posted by <a href="https://pybullet.org/Bullet/phpBB3/memberlist.php?mode=viewprofile&amp;u=742">CaptainNemo</a> — Fri Aug 18, 2006 7:59 pm</p><hr />
]]></content>
